<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>3.4.6: Practice</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m00765</md:content-id>
    <md:title>3.4.6: Practice</md:title>
    <md:uuid>f4857adb-8984-4ba0-b0bf-f26ad45ef117</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
    <section>
      <para>Complete the following questions to practice the skills you have learned in this lesson.</para>
      <section class="check-understanding">
        <exercise id="_2aeff761-3d80-478a-9dda-33e3b35ba77f" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>Select<emphasis>three</emphasis> values for \(r\) that indicate a positive slope for the line of best fit.</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! 1, 0.5, 0.8</para>
            <para>Try again. Revisit activity 3.4.2.</para>
            <para>The correct answers are 1, 0.5, 0.8.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="c15c992a-d18b-44e3-8338-3fc5472a48a6" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>Select<emphasis>three</emphasis> values for \(r\) that indicate a negative slope for the line of best fit.</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! –1, –0.87, –0.24</para>
            <para>Try again. Revisit activity 3.4.2.</para>
            <para>The correct answers are –1, –0.87, –0.24.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="_650178de-47e1-422c-ae0e-8df9073ec516" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>0.4, –0.85, 0.72, –0.31</para>
            <para>The correlation coefficient, \(r\), is given for several different linear models. Order the correlation coefficients as follows: start with the \(r\)-value indicating the strongest linear relationship and end with the \(r\)-value indicating the weakest linear relationship.</para>
            <para>Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para>\(0.72, 0.4, -0.31, –0.85\)</para>
            <para>\(–0.85, -0.31, 0.4, 0.72\)</para>
            <para>\(-0.31, 0.4, 0.72, –0.85, 0.72\)</para>
            <para>\(–0.85, 0.72, 0.4, -0.31\)</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! -0.85, 0.72, 0.4, -0.31 Correct! -0.85, 0.72, 0.4, -0.31</para>
            <para>Try again. Revisit activity 3.4.2.</para>
            <para>The correct answer is -0.85, 0.72, 0.4, -0.31.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="_08c73988-623d-42d1-bda5-b243c118c63b" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>–0.65, 0.47, –1, 0.89</para>
            <para>The correlation coefficient, \(r\), is given for several different linear models. Order the correlation coefficients as follows: start with the \(r\)-value indicating the strongest linear relationship and end with the \(r\)-value indicating the weakest linear relationship</para>
            <para>Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para>\(–1, 0.89, –0.65, 0.47\)</para>
            <para>\(0.47, -0.65, 0.89, -1\)</para>
            <para>\(–1, –0.65, 0.47, 0.89 \)</para>
            <para>\(0.89, 0.47, –1, –0.65, -1\)</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! –1, 0.89, –0.65, 0.47 Correct! –1, 0.89, –0.65, 0.47</para>
            <para>Try again. Revisit activity 3.4.2.</para>
            <para>The correct answer is –1, 0.89, –0.65, 0.47.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="_4bfb3f6f-a2a2-4a15-bf4d-96cb432567cd" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>5. Match the following scatter plots to the correct correlation coefficient from the following:</para>
            <para>\(r=0.67\)</para>
            <para>\(r=-0.33\)</para>
            <para>\(r=0.88\)</para>
            <para>\(r= -0.79\)</para>
            <para>
              <figure>
                <media alt="">
                  <image mime-type="image/jpeg" src="../../media/Algebra-1_03_06_13_01.jpg"/>
                </media>
              </figure>
           </para>
            <para>Scatter Plot A</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! \( r=0.88\)</para>
            <para>Try again. Revisit activities 3.4.4 – 3.4.5.</para>
            <para>The correct answer is \(r=0.88\).
     </para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="_38c1f1c2-30c8-4993-b195-0abf7718e8af" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>Scatter Plot B</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! \( r=-0.79\)</para>
            <para>Try again. Revisit activities 3.4.4 – 3.4.5.</para>
            <para>The correct answer is \(r=-0.79\).
     </para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="_1c8527d3-b1d6-4715-b044-0c29659d0e23" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>Scatter Plot C</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! \( r=-0.33\)</para>
            <para>Try again. Revisit activities 3.4.4 – 3.4.5.</para>
            <para>The correct answer is \(r=-0.33\).
     </para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="_8227ba2a-6275-45ef-a11a-4615f2355b91" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>Scatter Plot D</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! \(r=0.67\)</para>
            <para>Try again. Revisit activities 3.4.4 – 3.4.5.</para>
            <para>The correct answer is \(r=0.67\).
     </para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="_0e4d4f01-4909-40fc-a549-977860084877" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>6. Match the following scatter plots to the correct correlation coefficient from the following:</para>
            <para>\(r = 0.37\)</para>
            <para>\(r = 0.83\)</para>
            <para>\(r = -0.67\)</para>
            <para>\(r = -0.85\)</para>
            <para>
              <figure>
                <media alt="">
                  <image mime-type="image/jpeg" src="../../media/Algebra-1_03_06_13_02.jpg"/>
                </media>
              </figure>
           </para>
            <para>Scatter Plot A</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! \(r=-0.67\)</para>
            <para>Try again. Revisit activities 3.4.4 – 3.4.5.</para>
            <para>The correct answer is \(r=-0.67\).
     </para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="_6a8ac0a2-22f6-451f-99c3-8ddd2944851c" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>Scatter Plot B</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! \(r=0.83\)</para>
            <para>Try again. Revisit activities 3.4.4 – 3.4.5.</para>
            <para>The correct answer is \(r=0.83\).
     </para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="b3adcc1c-131b-421e-998d-86bd214426c5" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>Scatter Plot C</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! \(r=0.37\)</para>
            <para>Try again. Revisit activities 3.4.4 – 3.4.5.</para>
            <para>The correct answer is \(r=0.37\).
     </para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="_52a5ff65-f2e3-4bec-ba9a-822600f8b2fd" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>Scatter Plot D</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! \(r=-0.85\)</para>
            <para>Try again. Revisit activities 3.4.4 – 3.4.5.</para>
            <para>The correct answer is \(r=-0.85\).
     </para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="_0c572bab-4c76-49cd-b643-d03e1d90bfd4" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>7. Which of the following correlation coefficients would best describe this scatter plot?</para>
            <para>
              <figure>
                <media alt="SCATTER PLOT THAT SHOWS THE RELATIONSHIP BETWEEN AGE IN YEARS AND PRICE IN DOLLARS. THE SCATTER PLOT SHOWS A VERY STRONG NEGATIVE CORRELATION.">
                  <image mime-type="image/jpeg" src="../../media/Algebra-1_03_06_13_03.jpg"/>
                </media>
              </figure>
           </para>
            <para>Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para>-0.32</para>
            <para>0.87</para>
            <para>-0.87</para>
            <para>0.32</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! \(-0.87\)</para>
            <para>Try again. Revisit activities 3.4.2 – 3.4.5.
     </para>
            <para>The correct answer is \(-0.87\).
     </para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="e5ab9a38-a3da-4a5a-9ea2-ea0c48d44a0d" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>8. Which of the following correlation coefficients would best describe this scatter plot?</para>
            <para>
              <figure>
                <media alt="SCATTER PLOT THAT SHOWS THE RELATIONSHIP BETWEEN BODY MASS IN POUNDS AND BITE FORCE IN POUNDS. THE SCATTER PLOT SHOWS A STRONG POSITIVE CORRELATION.">
                  <image mime-type="image/jpeg" src="../../media/Algebra-1_03_06_13_04.jpg"/>
                </media>
              </figure>
           </para>
            <para>Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para>-0.62</para>
            <para>0.94</para>
            <para>-0.94</para>
            <para>0.62</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! 0.62</para>
            <para>Try again. Revisit activities 3.4.2 – 3.4.5.
     </para>
            <para>The correct answer is 0.62.
     </para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="f1067638-02fd-4a21-a383-8692cafdae54" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>9. Which of the following has the stronger linear relationship? Explain.</para>
            <para>Scatter Plot A:</para>
            <para>
              <figure>
                <media alt="SCATTER PLOT THAT SHOWS A MODERATE POSITIVE CORRELATION.">
                  <image mime-type="image/jpeg" src="../../media/Algebra-1_03_06_13_05.jpg"/>
                </media>
              </figure>
           </para>
            <para>Scatter Plot B:</para>
            <para>
              <figure>
                <media alt="SCATTER PLOT THAT SHOWS A STRONG POSITIVE CORRELATION.">
                  <image mime-type="image/jpeg" src="../../media/Algebra-1_03_06_13_06.jpg"/>
                </media>
              </figure>
           </para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! Scatter plot B because the points in the scatter plot are closer to forming a linear relationship.</para>
            <para>Try again. Revisit activity 3.4.2.
     </para>
            <para>The correct answer is scatter plot B because the points in the scatter plot are closer to forming a linear relationship.

     </para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="a9404ec6-8710-4e20-9345-d00023ddc075" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>10. Which of the following correlation coefficients would best describe the scatter plot?</para>
            <para>
              <figure>
                <media alt="SCATTER PLOT THAT SHOWS THE RELATIONSHIP BETWEEN FAT IN GRAMS AND CALORIES. THE SCATTER PLOT SHOWS A MODERATE POSITIVE CORRELATION.">
                  <image mime-type="image/jpeg" src="../../media/Algebra-1_03_06_13_07.jpg"/>
                </media>
              </figure>
           </para>
            <para>Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para>-0.89</para>
            <para>0.89</para>
            <para>0.43</para>
            <para>-0.43</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! 0.43</para>
            <para>Try again. Revisit activities 3.4.4 – 3.4.5.</para>
            <para>The correct answer is 0.43.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
      </section>
